We need to evaluate each claim against evidence. Provide verdicts list with id, supported true/false, reason short.

We have claims C1-C8, X1, X3. Let's check each.

C1: claim about subject details. Evidence includes tool summary profile_account and Q-ebdff3fe6c customer record. Both show institution A, name Peron & Lucas LLP, Partnership, FR, Retail clothing, risk Medium, PEP false, declared turnover $630,000. So supported.

C2: claim about inbound/outbound counts and totals. Evidence Q-b9a9fc1353 activity summary shows exactly those numbers. Supported.

C3: claim about outbound counterparties: 1 at A, 5 at B; largest is 10441:804C4B450 (B, Sole Proprietorship, ES, Agriculture, High risk) with 14 credit-card payments worth $59,878. Evidence tool summary get_counterparties says 1 at A, 5 at B, largest as described. Q-5c240d212f shows row for that counterparty with n_tx 14, usd_total 59877.72, institution B, customer_type Sole Proprietorship, country ES, occupation Agriculture, risk High. Claim says credit-card payments; top_format Credit Card. So supported.

C4: inbound counterparties: 3 at A, 4 at B; largest is 2591:80069D810 (B, Partnership, NL, Agriculture, Low risk) with 2 cheque payments worth $63,472. Evidence tool summary get_counterparties says 3 at A, 4 at B, largest as described. Q-34253f15c3 shows row with cp_bank 2591, cp_account 80069D810, n_tx 2, usd_total 63472.48, institution B, customer_type Partnership, country NL, occupation Agriculture, risk Low, top_format Cheque. Supported.

C5: follow-money out 2 hops shows 147 transactions to 6 accounts (1 A,5 B) then 108 transactions to 14 accounts (8 A,6 B) totalling $187,844, with 205 cross-institution transactions. Evidence tool summary follow_money says hop1 147 tx, 6 accounts (1 at A,5 at B), about $140,477; hop2 108 tx, 14 accounts (8 at A,6 at B), about $187,844; 205 cross-institution. Claim matches. Supported.

C6: follow-money in 2 hops shows 21 transactions from 7 accounts (3 A,4 B) then 34 transactions from 5 accounts (1 A,4 B) totalling $9.48M, with 35 cross-institution. Evidence tool summary follow_money says hop1 21 tx, 7 accounts (3 at A,4 at B), about $86,270; hop2 34 tx, 5 accounts (1 at A,4 at B), about $9,476,019; 35 cross-institution. Claim says $9.48M (close). Supported.

C7: inference that network analysis flags pass-through and burst as suspicious with given numbers. Evidence analyze_network shows pass_through suspicious with out/in ratio 1.63, 152% left within 72h; burst suspicious with 10 distinct counterparties, avg 1.3 per day, 7.6x. Supported.

C8: inference that no structural laundering signals present: no cycle, no layered transfers, no convergence, no interconnection, no uniform amounts, no high-volume hubs. Evidence analyze_network shows those signals all context 0/3 (strength 0). Also Q-6be5e169d4 shows 0 rows for cycles. So supported.

X1: claim outflows run at ~0.7× declared turnover ($425k vs $630k), consistent with normal business volume. Evidence profile_account says outflows run at about $425,538 a month, 0.7x declared turnover. Also turnover_vs_declared signal shows ratio 0.68. So supported.

X3: claim zero convergence or cycle detected; no single account collects from multiple subject counterparties and no funds return to subject. Evidence analyze_network shows convergence context 0/3, cycle context 0/3. Also Q-6be5e169d4 shows 0 rows for cycles. Supported.

All claims supported. Provide verdicts accordingly.</think>{
